[  18.9s] CORRECTED CONCLUSION (decomposing X by c=0 vs c≠0)
[  18.9s] ======================================================================
[  18.9s]    At a generic A, the fiber X_A := {(A', c) : g(A') = c·g(A)} decomposes:
[  18.9s] 
[  18.9s]    c ≠ 0 (rescale to c=1):
[  18.9s]      Tangent dim of c=1 fiber at (A'=A) = 1
[  18.9s]      Proportional fiber dim = 1   (the (ρ, 1/ρ) reparam line)
[  18.9s]      EXCESS non-proportional directions = 0
[  18.9s]      ⇒ The c=1 sub-fiber over generic A is EXACTLY the proportional locus.
[  18.9s]      ⇒ The c≠0 component of X_A is parameterised by (c, σ) — 2 dim.
[  18.9s] 
[  18.9s]    c = 0:
[  18.9s]      g(A') = 0 ⇔ A' ∈ V (zero-garbage variety, from zero_garbage_variety.py).
[  18.9s]      V is positive-dim, max component dim = 6 in (L', M') ∈ R^12.
[  18.9s]      ⇒ The c=0 component of X_A is V — 6 dim (max).
[  18.9s] 
[  18.9s]    Total: X has (at least) two irreducible components:
[  18.9s]      X_{proportional} : dim 12 (A) + 2 (fiber) = 14.
[  18.9s]      X_{c=0}          : dim 12 (A) + 6 (V max) = 18.
[  18.9s] 
[  18.9s] ======================================================================
[  18.9s] PROPORTIONALITY THEOREM (this script's main result)
[  18.9s] ======================================================================
[  18.9s]    For every (A, A', c) ∈ X with c ≠ 0:
[  18.9s]      A' is forced to come from a PROPORTIONAL rank-1 tensor.
[  18.9s]      I.e. ∃ ρ, σ ≠ 0 with L' = ρL/σ and M' = σM (so L'·M' = ρ·L·M, c=ρ).
[  18.9s] 
[  18.9s]    For (A, A', c) ∈ X with c = 0:
[  18.9s]      A' ∈ V; by zero_garbage_variety.py, α(A') = β(A') = 0.
[  18.9s] 
[  18.9s] ======================================================================
[  18.9s] IMPOSSIBILITY OF (2,2,bridge-3) IN THE RANK-1 ATOM FAMILY
[  18.9s] ======================================================================
[  18.9s]    A 3-atom (2, 2, bridge-3) construction needs the 28×3 garbage matrix
[  18.9s]    U = [g(A1) | g(A2) | g(A3)] to have rank ≤ 1, AND the (α, β) projections
[  18.9s]    to span Q ≅ R^2.
[  18.9s] 
[  18.9s]    rank(U) ≤ 1 means any two columns are proportional (allowing 0 columns).
[  18.9s]    For any i, j with g(A_i), g(A_j) both non-zero and proportional with
[  18.9s]    ratio c ≠ 0: by the proportionality theorem, A_i and A_j are themselves
[  18.9s]    proportional rank-1 tensors. So their (α, β) projections are proportional.
[  18.9s] 
[  18.9s]    For any column g(A_k) = 0: A_k ∈ V, so α(A_k) = β(A_k) = 0.
[  18.9s] 
[  18.9s]    ⇒ In any such triple, the (α, β) projections all lie on a single line
[  18.9s]      through the origin in Q. The (α, β) image has rank ≤ 1, cannot span Q.
[  18.9s] 
[  18.9s]    ⇒ NO (2, 2, bridge-3) construction exists in the rank-1 atom family.
[  18.9s] ======================================================================
